# Multilingual Synchronization Rules

- French at the root (`*.html`) is the primary source of truth for the website.
- Whenever any change (content, layout, structure, or design) is made, always apply it across all 3 languages: French (`*.html`), English (`en/*.html`), and Arabic (`ar/*.html`).
- Maintain full parity across all 3 versions, respecting `dir="rtl"` and proper translation context.

